                <pb facs="0307" n="301" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg301"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/5571: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé at Tangier (Childs) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-21T11:00:00+01:00">May 21, 1942—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 12:22 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>230. It may be perhaps useful to the Department to know that it is the unanimous
                    opinion of us here in Tangier including the Military and Naval Attachés as well
                    as my British colleague that at least token shipments should be resumed to
                    Morocco under the American-French economic accord.</p>
                <p>One obvious advantage of token shipments is that they offer a <hi
                        rendition="#italic">raison d’être</hi> for the continued activity of the
                    control officers whose reports have contributed so much to the work of
                    Anglo-American joint intelligence center here which is cooperating most
                    effectively with Gibraltar and Malta.</p>
                <p>By courier to Casablanca, Algiers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Childs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
